==Special Moves==
====Power Wave====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=terry_236A,terry_236C,terry_236AC
|input=236A/C/AC
|input2=qcf+A/C/AC
|description3=A projectile that travels along the ground. 
* The button pressed for it determines its startup and travel speed.
* REV version is instead a big wave that travels slowly along the ground, letting Terry approach.
* Holding C/AC transforms the move into a short-range energy blast similar to Round Wave from other games. Numbers in [brackets] indicate values that change when you hold C/AC.
A pretty alright projectile. Though you won’t be zoning too many people, it’s great for closing the gap, either of your own accord or by forcing the opponent to approach you instead. These are especially true in the case of the REV version, which is a big, slow fireball that locks the opponent down if they block it. 

If you hold the C or REV versions, this move becomes '''Burning Wave''', which is a short, stationary blast that is much better on block. When you do the REV version, it becomes a whopping +4, making it a great pressure reset. It’s good in corner juggles, too! 
}}

====Burning Knuckle====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=terry_214A,terry_214C,terry_214AC
|input=214A/C/AC
|input2=qcb+A/C/AC
|description3=Terry rushes straight at the opponent fist-first. 
* You can combo into the light version from 2A or Power Dunk Brake, and REV versions from heavies. Heavy version is too slow to combo from anything that isn’t a Wild Punish.
* All versions launch on Counter Hit.
* You can Brake the move to stop it short.
* More advantageous when properly spaced, use this farther out to avoid taking a big punish. 
Terry’s signature move. In neutral, it’s best used to approach behind fireballs, Brake to intimidate your opponent and possibly force reactions, and punish whiffs from a further distance than your normals allow.  

The light version combos from 2A and is your best meterless juggle when it’s available. The REV version is Terry’s go-to REV starter, since it combos from heavies and picks up combos nicely from Power Dunk brake, but some REV Accel sequences that combo on hit (namely to REV Crack Shoot) have gaps on block that can be mashed out of or worse, High Dodge Attacked, so it’s not as mindless a starter as it may seem. 

The heavy version is too slow to combo from anything reliably, but it makes up for it with massive damage and being the only version that can be made plus on block. If you manage to land a Counter Hit with it, such as when punishing a DP, it will hit like a freight train ''and'' launch into a full combo with no scaling, meaning you can easily take half their life or more with the ensuing combo. 
}}

